{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/656667-i-made-a-homebrew-family","id":656667,"title":"I Made a Homebrew Family :>","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Beast: The Primordial"],"posts":[{"date":"2015-09-08T10:15:08-07:00","id":656667,"title":"I Made a Homebrew Family :>","content":"Hello Dudes and Dudettes and people who don't fit in the gender binary. i was thinking to myself,Beast has the potential to have more splats,cause people have been havijng nightmares since the dawn of mankind,and there kinds of nightmares that were not explored in the game so here my take on one of them! (<a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1v-7uNxTuOVEyMJ0ixmvYfWoPZysOkLM0GJU915g-67Q/edit?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">https://docs.google.com/document/d/1...it?usp=sharing</a>) I made it like the splat session of the corebook,howeveri didn't come up with a birthright and stories section just yet,i will soon enough though. after that i'll submit to onyx path in the hope it goes to the beast players guide.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4621-nicolas-milioni","name":"Nicolas Milioni","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4621_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3605"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-08T14:49:47-07:00","id":656946,"title":"","content":"It needs some fine-tuning. Most of what this family does can be accomplished by other Beasts, so you need to come up with some mechanically distinct Atavisms and a unique Birthright. Also, could you show us how a Ravager of this Family acquires Satiety (I imagine explosives, loud music, and/or brightly painted, hyper-realistic murals might be involved <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" />).","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Crunch isn't a hobby; it's a calling.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1959-hexmeister-vic","name":"Hexmeister Vic","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1959_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"764"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-08T15:29:44-07:00","id":657022,"title":"","content":"This doesn't sound like a Family that can stand on its own. Sensory overload, synesthesia and the loss of distinction between pain and pleasure could all be achieved by Namtaru with the right Nightmares, if their effects are described in a Slaaneshi way. If you want to focus on violated senses in the form of deceitful hallucinations, a la Freddy Krueger, you can do that with Eshmaki. Extreme pain and pleasure that leave you incapable of moving or even thinking straight sounds like the sort of helplessness that Anakim would inflict. Psychosomatic hallucinations that make you relive your most traumatic experiences when you feel safe could be caused by Ugallu. Sensory deprivation and extreme temperatures sound fitting for the Makara.<br /> <br /> What I'm trying to say is that &quot;Nightmares Of The Senses&quot; is too broad and can be done by official Families with the right powers and narration. If you are not taking the time to describe the visceral impact of Nightmares on your victims, you aren't doing it right.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Bye.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4443-gibberingeloquence","name":"GibberingEloquence","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4443_5.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2470"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-08T17:54:57-07:00","id":657230,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>GottaGoFeast</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/656667-i-made-a-homebrew-family?p=657022#post657022\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">This doesn't sound like a Family that can stand on its own. Sensory overload, synesthesia and the loss of distinction between pain and pleasure could all be achieved by Namtaru with the right Nightmares, if their effects are described in a Slaaneshi way. If you want to focus on violated senses in the form of deceitful hallucinations, a la Freddy Krueger, you can do that with Eshmaki. Extreme pain and pleasure that leave you incapable of moving or even thinking straight sounds like the sort of helplessness that Anakim would inflict. Psychosomatic hallucinations that make you relive your most traumatic experiences when you feel safe could be caused by Ugallu. Sensory deprivation and extreme temperatures sound fitting for the Makara.<br /> <br /> What I'm trying to say is that &quot;Nightmares Of The Senses&quot; is too broad and can be done by official Families with the right powers and narration. If you are not taking the time to describe the visceral impact of Nightmares on your victims, you aren't doing it right.</div> </div> </div> </div>I think you might be missing something,Sensory overload and nightmares where your sense are assaulted can fall under the wings of others families but it's not the central aspect of the five core families nightmares,they can all cause sensory overload and make people lost the distinction between pain and pleasure,but it's not something necessary for the core families be what they are,it's not a vital part of the way they feed,the core families can <i>use </i>sensory overload,the Ashankwe <i>are </i>sensory overload. so i do think they can stand as aunique family,i hope you don't feel disrespected right now,i just don't agree on what you said on that criticism in particular.;","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4621-nicolas-milioni","name":"Nicolas Milioni","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4621_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3605"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-08T20:40:24-07:00","id":657326,"title":"","content":"Too much refinement for a rough-hewn Beast of Legend, too weak a basis for a Family category.<br /> <br /> Horrors are tearing skin in the water or a ululating howl in the night, with their form being relatively simple and inherently mutable over time; they don't have something so detailed and humanlike as art or instruments unless the Beast puts them there.<br /> <br /> People don't fear sensory overload. They fear drowning and falling and blindness and confinement and infection and unintended consequences and unforeseen complications and the innate untrustworthiness of the world around them. Sensory overload doesn't serve as a category of fear akin to the shadow of an imaginary predator \u2014 it's a very real phenomenon that it's all but impossible for the brain's pattern recognition to throw up a false positive.<br /> <br /> You seem to be after a Family tailor-made for Kinship with the Fae.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-08T21:13:29-07:00","id":657362,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Nicolas Milioni</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/656667-i-made-a-homebrew-family?p=657230#post657230\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I think you might be missing something,Sensory overload and nightmares where your sense are assaulted can fall under the wings of others families but it's not the central aspect of the five core families nightmares,they can all cause sensory overload and make people lost the distinction between pain and pleasure,but it's not something necessary for the core families be what they are,it's not a vital part of the way they feed,the core families can <i>use </i>sensory overload,the Ashankwe <i>are </i>sensory overload. so i do think they can stand as aunique family,i hope you don't feel disrespected right now,i just don't agree on what you said on that criticism in particular.;</div> </div> </div> </div> Hey, no problem. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /> It takes a whole lot for me to feel personally attacked or anything like that.<br /> <br /> As for what Satchel said, he's spot on. However, I like throwing curve balls at the characters who think they have the world all mapped out in a neat box. By which I mean, that there could be a recent Family based on the fear of technology embodying Change. I think the first glimpses of Beasts belonging to this Family were first seen some time after the start of the first Industrial Revolution, and after the advent of computers and the Internet, they grew rapidly in numbers. The things we are doing with technology and what technology is doing to us isn't just different from an unseen predator or debilitating disease on a visual level. It's thematically different because we did it, not nature. The Primordial Dream may not have fully acclimated itself to this new Family, as it plays by rules of ancient fears. But I believe the fear of change is distinctive enough for a new Family, not just an Anakim with a robotic Horror. It challenges the perceptions of the characters and it makes them wonder what else might be out there that they don't know. But since they're Beasts, they are probably smiling with shark teeth and guffawing with pestilent breath at this new addition to the Dark Mother's heirs. The more, the merrier.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Bye.","edited":{"userid":4443,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4443-gibberingeloquence","user":"GibberingEloquence","date":". 09-09-2015, 12:28 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4443-gibberingeloquence","name":"GibberingEloquence","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4443_5.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2470"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-08T22:00:42-07:00","id":657400,"title":"","content":"If I may make a suggestion, you could tweak the family to represent the <b>Fear of Ignorance</b>. They represent humanity's inability to comprehend the horror that threatens them. This could prompt a Hero to dedicate themselves to studying the Beast in an effort to learn more about them before going in for the kill. By the time you engage the Hero, they are both well armed and well prepared for the confrontation!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1394-nyrufa","name":"Nyrufa","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1394_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6374"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-09T18:38:36-07:00","id":658718,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Nyrufa</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/656667-i-made-a-homebrew-family?p=657400#post657400\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">If I may make a suggestion, you could tweak the family to represent the <b>Fear of Ignorance</b>. They represent humanity's inability to comprehend the horror that threatens them. This could prompt a Hero to dedicate themselves to studying the Beast in an effort to learn more about them before going in for the kill. By the time you engage the Hero, they are both well armed and well prepared for the confrontation!</div> </div> </div> </div>I tweaked them a bit like you said,i did include the faer of being ignorant as part of their nature,not the main part of the way they cause fear but a part of them nonetheless,good advice,i","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4621-nicolas-milioni","name":"Nicolas Milioni","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4621_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3605"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-09T18:39:16-07:00","id":658720,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Hexmeister Vic</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/656667-i-made-a-homebrew-family?p=656946#post656946\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">It needs some fine-tuning. Most of what this family does can be accomplished by other Beasts, so you need to come up with some mechanically distinct Atavisms and a unique Birthright. Also, could you show us how a Ravager of this Family acquires Satiety (I imagine explosives, loud music, and/or brightly painted, hyper-realistic murals might be involved <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" />).</div> </div> </div> </div>I'm having abit of writer's block with atavism,but i think when i do come up with some you might like it <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4621-nicolas-milioni","name":"Nicolas Milioni","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4621_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3605"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-14T12:11:18-07:00","id":664612,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>GottaGoFeast</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/656667-i-made-a-homebrew-family?p=657362#post657362\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> Hey, no problem. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /> It takes a whole lot for me to feel personally attacked or anything like that.<br /> <br /> As for what Satchel said, he's spot on. However, I like throwing curve balls at the characters who think they have the world all mapped out in a neat box. By which I mean, that there could be a recent Family based on the fear of technology embodying Change. I think the first glimpses of Beasts belonging to this Family were first seen some time after the start of the first Industrial Revolution, and after the advent of computers and the Internet, they grew rapidly in numbers. The things we are doing with technology and what technology is doing to us isn't just different from an unseen predator or debilitating disease on a visual level. It's thematically different because we did it, not nature. The Primordial Dream may not have fully acclimated itself to this new Family, as it plays by rules of ancient fears. But I believe the fear of change is distinctive enough for a new Family, not just an Anakim with a robotic Horror. It challenges the perceptions of the characters and it makes them wonder what else might be out there that they don't know. But since they're Beasts, they are probably smiling with shark teeth and guffawing with pestilent breath at this new addition to the Dark Mother's heirs. The more, the merrier.</div> </div> </div> </div>I forget who said it, but: &quot;The fear of the past was that men might become slaves, the fear of the future is that men might become robots&quot;.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\"><a href=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/personality.htm\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/pub/12.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a></div> &quot;A free society is one in which it is safe to be unpopular.&quot;<br /> <span style=\"color:DarkRed\"><span style=\"font-size:20px\"><span style=\"font-family:Comic Sans MS\">I find <a href=\"https://www.google.com/url?sa=t&amp;rct=j&amp;q=&amp;esrc=s&amp;source=web&amp;cd=3&amp;cad=rja&amp;uact=8&amp;ved=0ahUKEwin4NXQzLfXAhVGySYKHV3TDXYQFgg3MAI&amp;url=http%3A%2F%2Fwww.ign.com%2Farticles%2F2017%2F04%2F25%2Fmarvels-nick-spencer-on-captain-americas-betrayal-and-handling-fan-reactions&amp;usg=AOvVaw2EcsX7n5ebntygb0TizyGl\" target=\"_blank\">Nick Spencer</a> and <a href=\"https://www.google.com/url?sa=t&amp;rct=j&amp;q=&amp;esrc=s&amp;source=web&amp;cd=4&amp;cad=rja&amp;uact=8&amp;ved=0ahUKEwiK7d7szLfXAhXCWSYKHTpKBbcQFgg4MAM&amp;url=https%3A%2F%2Fen.wikipedia.org%2Fwiki%2FRichard_B._Spencer&amp;usg=AOvVaw1tuP6phfINia-bh_jWsDT_\" target=\"_blank\">Richard Spencer</a> to be equally repulsive.</span></span></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6138-mangle77","name":"Mangle77","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6138_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"605"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-14T12:20:00-07:00","id":664615,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>GottaGoFeast</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/656667-i-made-a-homebrew-family?p=657362#post657362\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> Hey, no problem. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /> It takes a whole lot for me to feel personally attacked or anything like that.<br /> <br /> As for what Satchel said, he's spot on. However, I like throwing curve balls at the characters who think they have the world all mapped out in a neat box. By which I mean, that there could be a recent Family based on the fear of technology embodying Change. I think the first glimpses of Beasts belonging to this Family were first seen some time after the start of the first Industrial Revolution, and after the advent of computers and the Internet, they grew rapidly in numbers. The things we are doing with technology and what technology is doing to us isn't just different from an unseen predator or debilitating disease on a visual level. It's thematically different because we did it, not nature. The Primordial Dream may not have fully acclimated itself to this new Family, as it plays by rules of ancient fears. But I believe the fear of change is distinctive enough for a new Family, not just an Anakim with a robotic Horror. It challenges the perceptions of the characters and it makes them wonder what else might be out there that they don't know. But since they're Beasts, they are probably smiling with shark teeth and guffawing with pestilent breath at this new addition to the Dark Mother's heirs. The more, the merrier.</div> </div> </div> </div> I like this idea very much! But what would we call them?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3514-zealouschristian24","name":"ZealousChristian24","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1796"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-14T15:01:22-07:00","id":664853,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Nicolas Milioni</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/656667-i-made-a-homebrew-family?p=658718#post658718\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I tweaked them a bit like you said,i did include the faer of being ignorant as part of their nature,not the main part of the way they cause fear but a part of them nonetheless,good advice,i</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> You're welcome. I gave it some thought and realized that the game is called Beast: the Primordial. All of the families so far have represented ancient fears of mankind's history. A fear of technology isn't exactly something that fits the bill here.<br /> <br /> But a fear of the unknown? A force beyond your comprehension that views you as prey? That is a very old fear, indeed. I dare say it's spurred human advancement all the way into the modern age and even beyond!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1394-nyrufa","name":"Nyrufa","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1394_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6374"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-14T20:40:34-07:00","id":665301,"title":"","content":"Ideas for sense-based Atavisms:<br /> <br /> Choking, blinding smoke<br /> Deafening roar<br /> Horrible stench<br /> Slimy, nauseating touch","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1419-wardragon","name":"WarDragon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1419_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1052"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-15T13:14:43-07:00","id":666026,"title":"","content":"Given the general nature of Families, the first thing I look at are the mechanics. In this case, I specifically look at the Birthrights. Birthrights tend to be almost extensions of a specific Atavism or Lair Trait. Something more towards the Beast side than the Nightmare-psychic side. Modifications to the self or the environment, in other words. Even the Namtaru Birthright, which makes people uneasy and lowers Composure, works in a similar manner to how the Looming Presence is terrifying, or Alien Allure makes everyone happy. I feel like the example Shutdown Birthright crosses the line from being monster-y into being a psychic attack. <br /> <br /> Same thing with the Nerve Claws. It feels like you're going with a psychic Beast, which I feel like should be the domain of Nightmares. Or using dreams/nightmares through exploring via Astral. I feel like Birthrights should be grounded in the phsyical instead of mental. <br /> <br /> That's my opinion, anyways. By all means, go for it if and ignore me if you're interested in that story, however.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2102-mcn","name":"MCN","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2102_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3479"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-24T10:51:42-07:00","id":676558,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MCN</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/656667-i-made-a-homebrew-family?p=666026#post666026\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Given the general nature of Families, the first thing I look at are the mechanics. In this case, I specifically look at the Birthrights. Birthrights tend to be almost extensions of a specific Atavism or Lair Trait. Something more towards the Beast side than the Nightmare-psychic side. Modifications to the self or the environment, in other words. Even the Namtaru Birthright, which makes people uneasy and lowers Composure, works in a similar manner to how the Looming Presence is terrifying, or Alien Allure makes everyone happy. I feel like the example Shutdown Birthright crosses the line from being monster-y into being a psychic attack.<br /> <br /> Same thing with the Nerve Claws. It feels like you're going with a psychic Beast, which I feel like should be the domain of Nightmares. Or using dreams/nightmares through exploring via Astral. I feel like Birthrights should be grounded in the phsyical instead of mental.<br /> <br /> That's my opinion, anyways. By all means, go for it if and ignore me if you're interested in that story, however.</div> </div> </div> </div> i did try to to make them attack people in a less physical way because what i'm going for is the fear everyone has of not being aware of the world around us,the fear of or mind playing trick on us and not being able to trust our senses,so a family based on this fear is iless physical than others. still,good advice though.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4621-nicolas-milioni","name":"Nicolas Milioni","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4621_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3605"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-11-30T15:18:15-08:00","id":1469273,"title":"","content":"um, its not there any more.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26173-evtrax","name":"evtrax","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date: